{{root|en|ine-pro|*peth₂-|*-iHnos}}
{{glossary|Adjective}} {{senseno|en|adj1}} is borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|Passer|t=bird genus}} (from {{der|en|la|passer|t=sparrow}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*peth₂-|t=to spread out; to fly (in the sense of spreading out wings)}}) + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ine|pos={{glossary|suffix}} meaning ‘of or pertaining to’}}.<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''n|id=138484|date=March 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj.'' and ''n}}</ref>

Adjective {{senseno|en|adj2}} is borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|passerinus|t=bird species}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ine}}. {{m|NL.||Passerinus}} is derived from {{der|en|la|passerīnus|t=of or fit for sparrows}}, from {{m|la|passer|t=sparrow}} (see above) + {{m|la|-īnus|pos=suffix  meaning ‘of or pertaining to’}}.<ref name="OED"/>

The {{glossary|noun}} is borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|Passerinae|t=former order of birds}}, a {{glossary|calque}} of {{der|en|fr|passereaux}},<ref name="OED"/> the {{glossary|plural}} of {{m|fr|passereau|t=sparrow; passerine (bird of the order Passeriformes)}}, from {{der|en|la|passer|t=sparrow}} (see above) + {{m|fr|-eau|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|diminutive}} {{glossary|masculine}} nouns, specifically the names of young animals}}.

